<!-- drawable/ic_pepito_tweaks.xml

     Pepito Tweaks: the PepitoLauncher mark inside a phone.

     The dot cluster is the stock Palm PVG100 launcher's mark, measured off the
     stock 8.1 Settings' own "Apps" row asset (res/drawable/ic_apps.png, 130x130)
     rather than eyeballed, so the arrangement is the real one: four large dots
     in a diamond, four small on the diagonals, two more at the poles. Two
     deliberate departures for a 24dp monochrome target - the source's horizontal
     pair sits 3/130 below centre, which is under a pixel here, so it is
     symmetrised; and the small dots are grown from 0.52x the large radius to
     0.60x so they still read at icon size. Stock drew it as a green gradient
     bitmap; monochrome vector here, tinted per the rest of the Lineage set.

     The frame is a compromise, not a measurement. The PVG100's 96.6 x 50.6 mm
     body is 1.909:1, but a frame that narrow starves the cluster - the fit turns
     width-limited and the dots shrink by a third. The outer rect is
     (5,1)-(19,23) = 14 x 22 = 1.571:1 instead, about halfway between true-Palm
     and the generic 16 x 20 phone outline, and incidentally the same bounds as
     Material's own smartphone icon. 1-unit stroke, so the cavity is
     (6,2)-(18,22); the inner corners are r=1 against the outer r=2 to stay
     concentric, since a square inner corner reads as a lump at this weight.

     The fit is still width-limited (0.35 units of side padding), so the ~2.2
     units of clearance above and below the poles fall out of it rather than
     being chosen. Redoing the cluster means redoing that fit - and note each
     dot's chord is twice its ROUNDED radius: round the two independently and the
     arc radius exceeds half the chord, which renders the circles as eggs.
-->
